# Synphony Deployment Finance OS — environment variables
#
# The MVP runs entirely on a local SQLite file (./data/synphony.db) and needs
# NO environment variables to run `npm run dev`. The variables below only
# matter once you swap in the production-grade services described in the
# README ("Replacing demo data" / "Next integrations").

# --- Database (optional) ----------------------------------------------------
# If unset, the app uses better-sqlite3 against ./data/synphony.db.
# Set this to a Postgres connection string to run against Postgres instead
# (see README "Deploying with Postgres" for the Drizzle config change needed).
# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@host:5432/synphony"

# --- Auth (optional, future) -------------------------------------------------
# The MVP uses a first-party cookie session (see src/lib/auth/session.ts) with
# bcrypt-hashed demo passwords seeded by `npm run db:seed`. To swap in a
# production auth provider (Supabase Auth, Clerk, NextAuth), add its required
# variables here, e.g.:
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=""
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=""
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=""

# --- Server Actions (optional, production deploys behind a proxy/CDN) ------
# NEXT_SERVER_ACTIONS_ENCRYPTION_KEY=""
